     In reference to a message posted by one@clinet.FI (Tero Valkonen) stating
the simplicity of ENDGAME because of teleportation...

     I don't know about you, Tero, but I could not teleport in ENDGAME. I was
eventually forced to circumvent the interior of ENDGAME (if you know what I
mean) which took quite a while. Regardless, a "mysterious force" always kept
me from teleporting...Fortunately, I tamed one of the wizards, so I managed to
make it through alive, but I would not say it were so very easy! I would have
liked more flashing lights and bells for the huge amount of hours I invested in
playing it, but I realize that, for a text-based game, there isn't much one
can do. In fact, I'm glad it was designed at way because I play it over a modem.
I must say that it a great game. I only wish I could explain the "fun of it" to
other people. "So, what you're saying is that you stay up all night playing this
game where all you do is kill monsters, get an amulet, and leave...And it's all
in ASCII? Sounds boring to me..."

     I do have a question, though. How does one go through a "hard" wall (other
than being, I guess, a Xorn)? I tried to tunnel and zap my way into the left
most rooms in the castle to no avail. I realize there is nothing there but 
dragons, but at the time I wanted to kill them for the "fun" of it.

